# === Per-deployment server config ===
# Written by GPUCONFIGURE.bat → gpu-configure.html admin UI.
# Each operator picks their own resource tier; host-specific.
server/resource-config.json

# === T18.12 per-machine runtime artifact ===
# autoClearStaleState() writes SHA256 of the brain-logic source files
# to this file on every boot. Compared against the prior-boot value to
# decide whether to preserve or clear state. Per-machine + per-boot
# runtime data; must not be committed. Each clone computes its own
# hash on first boot.
server/brain-code-hash.json

# === T18.37 per-machine runtime log ===
# start.bat + Savestart.bat redirect node brain-server.js stdout/stderr
# to server/server.log so operators can tail heartbeat + brain info even
# if the launcher terminal goes invisible (Windows Terminal rendering
# glitches). Per-boot runtime data; must not be committed.
server/server.log

# === 114.19es.5 dictionary disk cache ===
# definition-service.js writes K-VOCAB definitions fetched from
# dictionaryapi.dev to this file every 5 min during runs and on graceful
# shutdown. Per-machine runtime cache (grows up to ~10k entries / few MB);
# rebuilds organically on cache miss + API fetch. Not load-bearing, not
# committable.
server/definition-cache.json
server/boot-error.log

# === Claude Code — .claude/ IS TRACKED HERE, BY OPERATOR DECISION ===
#
# The blanket `.claude/` exclude that used to sit here was REMOVED 2026-09-01.
# It was ignoring 497 of 521 files in the tree while 24 legacy files stayed
# tracked from before it landed — so the repo held a broken half of the
# workflow, and the ignore rule read as protection while doing nothing about
# the files already in the index.
#
# Gee (verbatim, 2026-07-04, the original authorization): "option 3, we want
# people to see how we got to where we aare with the project so they need
# workflow and files of .claude"
#
# Gee (verbatim, 2026-09-01, reaffirming when this was queried): "the brain
# project folder is entirely shipped to both repos, im telling you this now so
# what ever is telling u not to push it to both remotes is inaccurat and needs
# ajustment"
#
# This repo is on the `OPERATOR_AUTHORIZED_PUBLIC_REPOS` allowlist inside
# .claude/hooks/pre-tool-public-repo-guard.cjs — the sanctioned per-repo
# carve-out to the IP-boundary LAW. The hook returns a synthetic PASS here and
# would never have blocked a push. See .claude/CONSTRAINTS.md §LAW — .CLAUDE
# WORKFLOW IP BOUNDARY.
#
# WHAT STAYS IGNORED, and why each one:

# 159 MB of third-party TTS binaries across 365 files — two 63 MB .onnx voice
# models, a 9 MB onnxruntime.dll, espeak dictionaries. NOT workflow IP, and git
# keeps blobs forever: committing this would permanently add ~159 MB to both
# remotes with no way back except a history rewrite. Fetched by its own setup,
# not authored here.
.claude/piper/

# Personal + machine-local. Anthropic-default-gitignored anyway; listed
# explicitly because the blanket rule that used to cover them is gone.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.env
.claude/user.json
.claude/user-context/

# Auth key. .claude/CONSTRAINTS.md says of this file: "user auth key, never
# touch" — it must never reach a remote, public or private.
.claude/pollinations-user.json

# Regenerated every session by the hooks; machine-local absolute paths and
