# === iter13 hippocampal consolidation runtime state ===
# server/schemas.json — Tier 2 schematic memory (concept abstractions
# built from cosine-grouped episodes). Derivative state — wiped on
# auto-clear, rebuilt by ConsolidationEngine on next dream cycle.
# Per-machine + per-session runtime data.
server/schemas.json
# server/teachview-state.json — the persisted TEACH VIEW: what has been taught,
# per lane, per cell, plus a bounded reading ring. Per-machine runtime state
# describing THIS box's walk, so it is never committed. Wiped by
# autoClearStaleState on a fresh walk (it counts what was taught into weights
# that no longer exist) and kept across a Savestart, which is the retention it
# was built for.
server/teachview-state.json
# server/identity-core.json — Tier 3 identity-bound permanent attractors
# (Unity's core self: name/age/persona/biographical anchors). EXCLUDED
# from autoClearStaleState wipe list — survives code updates, fresh
# boots, drug states. Per-machine permanent runtime data containing
# user-specific consolidated memories. Each operator's Unity grows
# her own identity over time; never committed.
server/identity-core.json
server/identity-core.json.tmp
server/identity-core.json.corrupt-*
# server/mindspace-memory.json — UVM-INT.4 imagined field-C ring (the ".uvme
# medium" memory). Derivative per-machine runtime imagery; re-imagined if lost.
server/mindspace-memory.json
server/mindspace-memory.json.tmp
# server/visual-memory.json — TU.29.5 seen-concept field-C store (visual memory
# medium — derivative brain state, recreated as she sees; never committed)
server/visual-memory.json
server/visual-memory.json.tmp

# === PA.4.8 community-compute tier marker ===
# Persisted by the milestone execution gate; read at boot to scale the brain
# to the donor-pool community tier. Per-machine runtime state — never committed.
server/community-tier.json

# === LANGRAM.6 language-cortex geometry pin ===
# The size the language cortex was TRAINED at, written on every boot and held on
# later ones so a boot-time free-RAM dip cannot silently resize the vocabulary
# ceiling underneath weights sized for the old geometry. Per-machine runtime
# state — never committed. DREAM_LANG_CORTEX / DREAM_LANG_UNPIN / a fresh walk
# are the three ways to change it, all loud.
server/lang-geometry.json

# === TOPOPIN — intra-synapse wiring pin (2026-08-25) ===
# Records whether this brain was BUILT with topographic (1-D ring) or
# random-global connectivity, so a Savestart resume cannot flip the wiring
# underneath weights trained with the other topology — the same failure the
# geometry pin above exists to prevent. Per-machine runtime state, never
# committed: a brain built on one box says nothing about a brain on another.
# A FRESH WALK re-decides and rewrites it (the pin binds resumes only);
# DREAM_TOPOGRAPHIC=0/1 always wins for a deliberate change.
server/brain-topology.json

# === DF.7 community-compute auto-scale settings ===
# Admin-set toggle + dead-zone buffer + stability window for the milestone
# auto-resize. Persisted by /autoscale POST. Per-deployment runtime state.
server/autoscale-settings.json

# === DF.7 auto-advance toggle (standalone) ===
# Persisted separately from brain-weights so the auto-advance setting survives a
# tier resize/downscale weight-clear → unattended re-walks. Per-deployment.
server/auto-advance.json

# === PA.4.2 primary-operator binding ===
# First Forgejo-authed operator after deploy is bound here (locked + persisted
# across reboots → guarantees the operator stays master on a static deploy).
# Per-deployment runtime state — never committed, never auto-cleared.
server/operator-identity.json

# === Corpora (auto-downloaded by start.bat / start.sh) ===
# GloVe 6B.300d ~990 MB plain text — way too big for git. Auto-fetched
# from Stanford NLP on first run per corpora/README.md. Never commit.
corpora/glove.6B.300d.txt
corpora/glove.6B.zip
corpora/glove.6B.*.txt

# ⛔⛔ THE CORPUS LIVES IN ONE REPO, AND IT IS NOT THIS ONE.
#
# Operator: *"we need to makes suure there is only one repo with all the corpus
# and fields, PERIOD! Then when it auto downloads it to the server when pressing
# update freshwalk the server then trains Unity on it as the books and
# information that trains her via pgase cell grade course ciriculim corpus....
# directly"*.
#
# The books and the wavelet fields now both live in `UnityAILab/BrainWaves`,
# and `deploy/self-update.sh` pulls BOTH from there on every press — `corpora`
# is on that script's rsync exclude list so a code overlay can never overwrite
# the data. Tracking a second copy here is precisely the drift he was objecting
# to: this one was already stale against the data repo, in both directions.
#
# ⚠ THE FILES STAY ON DISK LOCALLY — this is `git rm --cached`, not a delete.
# The fetchers and `audit-curriculum-coverage.mjs` still read `corpora/` here;
# what changed is that the result is published by copying into the data repo and
# pushing THAT, instead of committing a duplicate into the code repo.
#
# ⚠ STATED COST, so it is chosen rather than discovered: a clone of this
# repository — including the PUBLIC one — no longer carries the books. Anyone
# running the walk locally needs the data repo alongside it.
corpora/

