# === Temp & cache ===
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.temp
# Corpus cell files are written to a temp sibling and renamed, so two ingests
# running at once cannot leave a half-written cell behind. `*.tmp` above does not
# match — the suffix carries the writing process's pid so two runs cannot collide
# on the temp name either — and a crashed run leaves one of these next to a
# tracked corpus file.
*.tmp-[0-9]*
*.log
*.cache
.cache/
.parcel-cache/

