# ── Fable Kit — OPERATOR TOOLING, not project source ─────────────────────────
# A third-party kit (protocol launcher + LLM-maintained codebase wiki + central
# vault) installed to browse THIS stack. The kit itself lives outside the repo
# in ~/.claude/; these are the only artefacts that land in the project folder.
#
# ⛔ Ignored on the same principle that removed the ai-ministries CLI plugin:
# tooling that helps someone READ the brain is not part of the brain, and the
# repo is the brain. A wiki/ of generated pages beside docs/ would also give
# the project two doc trees with different rules, and docs/ is the one the
# LAWs govern.
#
# ⚠ Ignoring wiki/ does NOT break its staleness check: `last-verified` hashes
# and every path in a page's `sources:` refer to TRACKED files, so
# `git diff <hash>..HEAD -- <sources>` resolves exactly the same.
wiki/
fable-kit.zip
fable-kit/
graphify-out/

# Stray screenshots dropped at the repo root. `Stack Vault.png` (3.0 MB) was
# committed by a `git add -A` and sat tracked for a day, and the only thing that
# noticed was the vault's file-coverage number reading 99.8% — a wiki page names
# every other file in the tree, so one un-nameable binary is exactly what shows.
# Root only: server/shot-*.png above is a real capture path and stays.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp

# Default --out path for the figure generator. A run started without an
# explicit --out lands here; it is generated output and never belongs in git.
# (One was committed by accident on 2026-09-02 when an ESM "does it load" check
# executed the script.)
server/corpus-figures.db/
